From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cam <cam@x.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-microsoft-denali: exclude the unbound IR
 camera

CAMSS enumerates every described endpoint and waits for all of them
before it completes registration. The IR sensor VD55G0 has no usable
driver, so it never binds and CAMSS creates no sensor media links for
any of the three cameras. The rear OV13858 and the front IMX681 bind,
but with zero links, and userspace sees no camera.

Remove the IR endpoint from CAMSS port 0 and disable the IR sensor node
and its CCI0 bus 0, so that registration covers the two RGB sensors
only: rear on CCI0 bus 1 and front on CCI1 bus 1. The fragment is
included only by the m15-safe fallback and the variants that build on
it, not by the packaged DTS.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-camera-no-ir.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-camera-no-ir.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-camera-no-ir.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-camera-no-ir.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4110dd284063
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-camera-no-ir.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/* Exclude the unsupported IR endpoint from CAMSS's async notifier. */
+&camss {
+	ports {
+		/delete-node/ port@0;
+	};
+};
+
+&ir_camera {
+	status = "disabled";
+	/delete-node/ port;
+};
+
+&cci0_i2c0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
--
2.43.0
